<iscomment>
    Topsort sponsored banner, as a Page Designer component.

    Used for the three home page slots. The merchandiser drops one of these into the hero
    carousel slides region for home-slider-5 and home-slider-6, and into the full width row
    for home-banner-full; the slot attribute is what decides which auction runs.

    The banner comes in through a remote include so the home page keeps its page cache. When
    no campaign wins, the fragment removes the wrapper Page Designer puts around this
    component, which is what stops an empty slide appearing in the carousel.
</iscomment>
<isscript>
    // Registered from here rather than from the fragment. A remote include renders no
    // decorator, so an assets.addCss inside it would be collected and then thrown away with
    // the fragment's own request - the stylesheet has to be asked for by the page. On the
    // home page nothing else pulls it in, because there is no product grid.
    require('*/cartridge/scripts/assets').addCss('/css/topsort-sponsored.css');
</isscript>
<isif condition="${pdict.isEditMode}">
    <div class="ts-banner-placeholder">
        <span class="ts-banner-placeholder__title">Topsort - Sponsored Banner</span>
        <span class="ts-banner-placeholder__slot">${pdict.slotId}</span>
        <span class="ts-banner-placeholder__hint">Filled at runtime by the winning campaign for this slot. Nothing renders when no campaign wins.</span>
    </div>
<iselse/>
    <isinclude url="${URLUtils.url('Topsort-Banner', 'slotId', pdict.slotId)}" />
</isif>
